  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts and it passes typecheck. I couldn't run it in a browser or build it, so nothing has been seen on screen, including whether the soldier faces its direction of travel. The scene loads /assets/soldier.glb at 1.8 m tall and loops `Walk`. The soldier moves on a radius-4 circle around the origin, with its yaw set from the path tangent each frame. Pressing `r` crossfades to `Run` over 0.35 s and eases the travel speed from 1.4 m/s up to 3.6 m/s. Pressing `w` goes back to `Walk` the same way. The scene has a ground plane, a ring marking the path, a neutral environment, and a directional light with `shadow: true`. A fixed perspective camera at [0, 8.5, 9.5] frames the whole circle. `__EVAL_READY__` is set after the app is ready and two animation frames have passed. Two assumptions to check when you view it:\n- **Facing:** I assumed the model's forward axis is +Z. If the soldier walks backwards or sideways, change `MODEL_YAW_OFFSET`.\n- **Hash:** `defineModelAssets` needs a SHA-256 of the file and I couldn't compute one by hand. The code fetches the GLB at startup and hashes it in the browser, which costs one extra download of the file.",
